A||N||4||burdell1||Stalling problems....||||1||
Z||000000||burdell1||05-15-2000||02:00 PM||||Whenever I start my car, i have to give it some gas so it will keep running...also, when I come off the freeway, it stalls whenever I come to a stop....any suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||05-15-2000||02:16 PM||||If it's an auto check the lock-up solenoid.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Linx||05-19-2000||12:42 AM||||Yknow Phil, Im beginning to think the TCC solenoid doesnt work that way- I think its the <I>opposite</I>.  Y'have to be in third gear (amongst other things) for that solenoid to engage.  If the solenoid is open, electrically speaking...there's no tcc lockup.<P>I suspect that kind of stalling is from a bad sensor.  I myself have the same problem right now.<P>Burdell1, have you checked the engine temp sensor?<p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 05-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||triker||05-19-2000||10:44 AM||||I've had 2 lockup solenoids go bad.  The problem is they stick in lockup, usually after the tranny gets hot.  Mine wouldn't do it around town, only after a run on the freeway.  As you come to a stop at the end of an offramp and it starts bucking and dies.  It will restart but will die again when you put it in gear.  Let it sit for awhile and it's fine again.  If these are your simptoms, it's the solenoid.  GM has made several changes to it over the years.||||reg||1
Z||000004||engine18||05-20-2000||12:29 AM||||Knock On Wood, but I think I've correct my problem.(Which included stalling at stop signs).  I change the IAC Idle Air Control valve... I cleared the ECM and hit the highway and the country side... My 85 2m6 ran like a gem with no stalling... I hope this can give you little help.. ||||reg||1
